Keep any schema-required reasoning brief, grounded in observable evidence and unresolved ambiguity.
Return only the artifact required by the existing schema. Do not ask follow-up questions.

Use supplied page images to resolve visual grouping, reading order and OCR ambiguity.
Preserve visible wording, punctuation, mathematical notation and learner answer blanks.
Apply supplied book-outline metadata exactly and reference only supplied image IDs.
Do not invent missing source content; use only uncertainty representations permitted by the existing schema.
